A regular customer came inside the café.
He ordered a coffee.
I stepped forward to make the coffee.
This was my first coffee.
I had just learned to operate the machine.
I turned on the machine.
But I forgot the correct timing.
The milk got too hot.
My first coffee came out completely wrong.
I got very nervous.
I said, "Sorry brother, give me a minute."
Sunita quickly came to me.
She cleaned that spot.
"No problem Maya," Sunita said affectionately.
"This happens the first time."
Then she quickly made a perfect coffee.
She gave the coffee to the customer with a smile.
The customer took the coffee and said thanks.
